## psc/parse/stmt/values.pengu — constructos con valor.
##
## Implementa los hooks `PsHooks.value`, `when`, `do_block`, `with_init`,
## `or_block` y `when_body`. Vive por encima de `stmt/core` y `expr/ops`; el
## parser de expresiones lo llama a través de `PsHooks`, así no hay imports
## cíclicos.
##
## ## Memoria
## Construye nodos en el AST; no asigna strings salvo diagnósticos.

import psc.span as pspan
import psc.source as psource
import psc.token as pstoken

import psc.ast.kind as pskind
import psc.ast.node as psast
import psc.parse.state as psstate
import psc.parse.diagnostics as pdiag
import psc.parse.expr.ops as pexpr
import psc.parse.stmt.core as pstmt

insignia psc_parse_value_

## Hook `value`: `if`/`unless`/`while`/`for` en posición de valor.
##
## ## Memoria
## Construye el nodo correspondiente.
weave pvalues_parse_value with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwIf:
        return calling pvalues_parse_if with p
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwUnless:
        return calling pstmt.pstmt_parse_unless with p
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwWhile:
        return calling pstmt.pstmt_parse_while with p
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwFor:
        return calling pvalues_parse_for with p
    var off as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    calling ps_emit_here with p, pdiag.ParseIssue.ParseExpectedExpression, ""
    return calling ps_error_node with p, off, off

## Parsea `if` como expresión (`then`) o como statement con bloque.
##
## ## Memoria
## Construye `if_expr` o `if_stmt`.
weave pvalues_parse_if with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var start as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    var ignored as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwIf, "'if'"
    # La forma de binding solo existe en el statement.
    if calling ps_check_name_like with p:
        if (calling ps_kind_ahead with p, 1) == TokKeyword:
            if (calling ps_kw_at_offset with p, 1) == KwAs:
                var cond as int is calling pstmt.pstmt_parse_if_cond with p
                return calling pstmt.pstmt_parse_if_tail with p, start, cond
    var cond2 as int is calling pexpr.pexpr_parse_expr with p
    if calling ps_check_word with p, "then":
        var ignored2 as bool is calling ps_accept_word with p, "then"
        var then_value as int is calling pexpr.pexpr_parse_expr with p
        var ignored3 as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwElse, "'else'"
        var else_value as int is calling pexpr.pexpr_parse_expr with p
        calling ps_begin_children with p
        calling ps_add_child with p, cond2
        calling ps_add_child with p, then_value
        calling ps_add_child with p, else_value
        return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdIfExpr, start, (calling pexpr.pexpr_end_of with p, else_value), 0
    # Forma statement: envolver la condición ya parseada en `if_cond`.
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    calling ps_add_child with p, cond2
    var ic as int is calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdIfCond, (calling pexpr.pexpr_start_of with p, cond2), (calling pexpr.pexpr_end_of with p, cond2), 0
    return calling pstmt.pstmt_parse_if_tail with p, start, ic

## Parsea `for` como comprehension o como statement.
##
## ## Memoria
## Construye `for_comp` o delega en `pstmt_parse_for`.
weave pvalues_parse_for with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    # Rango y forma con dos nombres: el statement de core.
    if calling ps_check_name_like_at with p, 1:
        var n2 as TokenKind is calling ps_kind_ahead with p, 2
        if n2 == TokKeyword:
            var nkw as KeywordKind is calling ps_kw_at_offset with p, 2
            if nkw == KwFrom:
                return calling pstmt.pstmt_parse_for with p
        if n2 == TokComma:
            return calling pstmt.pstmt_parse_for with p
    var start as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    var ignored as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwFor, "'for'"
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    calling pvalues_add_name with p
    var ignored2 as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwIn, "'in'"
    var iterable as int is calling pexpr.pexpr_parse_expr with p
    calling ps_add_child with p, iterable
    var has_cond as bool is false
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwWhen:
        var ignored3 as Token is calling ps_advance with p
        var cond as int is calling pexpr.pexpr_parse_expr with p
        calling ps_add_child with p, cond
        set has_cond is true
    if calling ps_check_word with p, "then":
        if not has_cond:
            calling ps_add_absent with p
        var ignored4 as bool is calling ps_accept_word with p, "then"
        var body as int is calling pexpr.pexpr_parse_expr with p
        calling ps_add_child with p, body
        return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdForComp, start, (calling pexpr.pexpr_end_of with p, body), 0
    # Statement `for NAME in iterable:`.
    if has_cond:
        calling ps_emit_here with p, pdiag.ParseIssue.ParseUnexpectedToken, "'when' in a for statement"
    var blk as int is calling pstmt.pstmt_parse_block with p
    calling ps_add_child with p, blk
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdForInStmt, start, (calling ps_previous_end with p), 0

## Añade el nombre del loop al nodo en construcción.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave pvalues_add_name with p as ref to PsParser into void:
    calling ps_add_name_like with p

## Hook `when`: `when ... then ... else ...` o `when ...:` statement.
##
## ## Memoria
## Construye `when_expr` o `when_stmt`.
weave pvalues_parse_when with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var start as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    var ignored as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwWhen, "'when'"
    var cond as int is calling pexpr.pexpr_parse_expr with p
    if calling ps_check_word with p, "then":
        var ignored2 as bool is calling ps_accept_word with p, "then"
        var then_value as int is calling pexpr.pexpr_parse_expr with p
        var ignored3 as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwElse, "'else'"
        var else_value as int is calling pexpr.pexpr_parse_expr with p
        calling ps_begin_children with p
        calling ps_add_child with p, cond
        calling ps_add_child with p, then_value
        calling ps_add_child with p, else_value
        return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdWhenExpr, start, (calling pexpr.pexpr_end_of with p, else_value), 0
    var blk as int is calling pstmt.pstmt_parse_block with p
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    calling ps_add_child with p, cond
    calling ps_add_child with p, blk
    if calling ps_check_kw with p, KwElse:
        var eb as int is calling pstmt.pstmt_parse_when_else with p
        calling ps_add_child with p, eb
    else:
        calling ps_add_absent with p
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdWhenStmt, start, (calling ps_previous_end with p), 0

## Hook `do_block`: `do:` como expresión.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea un nodo `do_expr` con `stmt` hijos.
weave pvalues_parse_do with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var start as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    var ignored as bool is calling ps_accept_word with p, "do"
    var ignored2 as Token is calling ps_expect with p, TokColon, "':'"
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    calling pstmt.pstmt_parse_block_body_into with p
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdDoExpr, start, (calling ps_previous_end with p), 0

## Hook `with_init`: `with:` como expresión.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea un nodo `with_init_expr` con `stmt` hijos.
weave pvalues_parse_with_init with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    var start as int is calling ps_current_start with p
    var ignored as Token is calling ps_expect_kw with p, KwWith, "'with'"
    var ignored2 as Token is calling ps_expect with p, TokColon, "':'"
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    calling pstmt.pstmt_parse_block_body_into with p
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdWithInitExpr, start, (calling ps_previous_end with p), 0

## Hook `or_block`: `or:` con el lado izquierdo ya parseado.
##
## El parser de expresiones ya consumió `or`; el `:` sigue siendo actual.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea un nodo `or_block`.
weave pvalues_parse_or_block with p as ref to PsParser, left as int into int:
    var start as int is calling pexpr.pexpr_start_of with p, left
    calling ps_begin_children with p
    calling ps_add_child with p, left
    calling pstmt.pstmt_parse_block_into with p
    return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdOrBlock, start, (calling ps_previous_end with p), 0

## Hook `when_body`: cuerpo de una cláusula `when ... -> ...`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve la expresión, o un `do_expr` con el bloque.
weave pvalues_parse_when_body with p as ref to PsParser into int:
    if calling ps_check with p, TokNewline:
        if (calling ps_kind_ahead with p, 1) == TokIndent:
            var start as int is calling ps_current_start with p
            var ignored as Token is calling ps_advance with p
            var ignored2 as Token is calling ps_expect with p, TokIndent, "indent"
            calling ps_begin_children with p
            var more as bool is true
            while more:
                calling ps_skip_newlines with p
                if (calling ps_check with p, TokDedent) or (calling ps_check with p, TokEof):
                    set more is false
                else:
                    var before as int is p->pos
                    var st as int is calling pstmt.pstmt_parse_stmt with p
                    calling ps_add_child with p, st
                    if p->pos == before:
                        var forced as Token is calling ps_advance with p
            if calling ps_check with p, TokDedent:
                var ignored3 as Token is calling ps_advance with p
            return calling ps_finish_node with p, NodeKind.NdDoExpr, start, (calling ps_previous_end with p), 0
    var expr as int is calling pexpr.pexpr_parse_expr with p
    if calling ps_check with p, TokNewline:
        var ignored4 as Token is calling ps_advance with p
    return expr
